# Linux containers are built from this tree on Windows workstations, and a
# CRLF shebang is fatal: the kernel looks for an interpreter named "/bin/bash\r"
# and the container dies with "No such file or directory" and exit 127 — an
# error that points at the script rather than at its line endings.
#
# CRLF in sshd_policy.conf is subtler and worse: it puts a stray \r into the
# algorithm lists sshd parses, so the node's advertised SSH policy could
# silently stop matching the proxy's.
#
# Force LF for everything that a Linux process has to read.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.ndjson    text eol=lf

*.png       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.joblib    binary
*.pkl       binary
